      },
      "created_at": "2025-03-31T19:17:49.730Z",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "@Nicole Weber we could use the \"Name\" field for an accessible label for the field (while the URL in it would be a \"value\" and would still be announced). What is shown when there is nothing entered in the URL bar? options that come to mind:\n1. We could use this string as a \"Name\": i.e. on-screen placeholder is \"Search or enter an address\" - it would be a name and a VoiceOver would announce the URL bar from the example here as: \"Search or enter an address, theverge dot com, Text field\". - I like this is visible on-screen at some point, but it's long\n2. Safari uses \"Address\" as a \"Name\" and the example would be announced as \"Address, theverge dot com, Text field\" - I like that it's short\n3. We could use \"URL\" as a name too: \"URL, theverge dot com, Text field\" - it may be too technical for some users (I am not a context designer though, I do not know how familiar users are with this term)",
