      "message": "@Nicole Weber a screen reader would announce it as \"Shield secure connection\". I am not sure \"shield\" word is adding information here, but since it's not a control (we cannot tap it to open a dialog, right?) it is not required by WCAG 2.2 to include it as a visual label at the beginning of the textual alternative. Trying to say that \"Shield secure connection\" would be equally accessible as \"Secure connection\" for this image.\n\nAlso, could you please add \"Role: Image\" in the note here?",
